    "\n",
    "* Encode / Decode (The Rules): This is a fixed, non-trainable mapping. It translates characters to numbers purely because computers can't read. It is rigid: 'h' is always 12, and 12 is always 'h'. The encoder doesn't know what a word means; it is just a translator.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Embedding Table (The Brain): This is a grid of adjustable weights. It doesn't translate characters to integers; it takes an integer (like 12) and looks up how much the model likes every other character after it. The numbers in this table change constantly during training as the model learns grammar.\n",
